  "note": "The 2nd, 5th and 1st chords of a key as small triads, one per beat on the top three strings and then one string set lower, in a play-along with the tab. The chords are tokens (in the title too), counted the long way the first time, the shapes carry their key, so the old Am, D and G copy is now moves (any key, 66 to 90 bpm); each block has its feel to reach, the first named as muscle memory.",
